DParser for Python
==================

The Python binding lets you write a whole parser in Python: each function
whose name starts with d_ is an action, and its docstring holds the grammar
rules it is the action for.

Install, from the top of the DParser source tree:

  pip install .

Documentation (https://jplevyak.github.io/dparser/):

  Tutorial:       https://jplevyak.github.io/dparser/tutorial/python/
  API reference:  https://jplevyak.github.io/dparser/reference/python/
  Attributes:     https://jplevyak.github.io/dparser/reference/attributes/

Examples are in python/tests/.  To run them:

  PYTHONPATH=python python3 -m pytest python/tests

index.html and py_dparser_manual.html are the original documentation; the
pages above supersede them.

The binding was created by Brian Sabbey.  Thanks to Brennan Evans for more
general Unix support, Milosz Krajewski for non-Unix support and directory
independence, and Yves Forkl for bug reports, usability suggestions, and
the Emacs Lisp code to jump to syntax error locations.
